                <pb facs="0725" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg655"/>

                <head>No. 403.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-30"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 30, 1883</date>.
                        (Received June 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 634.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I telegraphed you to day as follows:
                    “Consul at Mazatlan telegraphs that Captain Caleb is provided with competent
                    counsel in appellate court.”</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
